Description: official tldr client written in Rust (tlrc)
 tldr shows simplified, example-driven help pages for command-line tools, taken
 from the community-maintained tldr-pages project. This package ships tlrc, the
 official Rust client: a single static binary with an offline, self-updating
 page cache, platform-specific and translated pages, and a configurable output.
 .
 The command is tldr. The package includes the man page and shell completions
 for bash, fish and zsh. The first run downloads the pages cache from the
 internet.
